body:
Asked for by the maintainer in chat, 2026-11-17:

> "we should be able to "Save" panel setups what is opened, where they are attached and how."

The maintainer set the priority `P3` in the same message.

What is wanted: the user can save the panel setup of the window and get it back later. A saved panel setup holds:

- which panels are open;
- where each panel is attached (the dock side or area, or a floating window with its position);
- how each panel is attached (its size, its tab order, its collapsed state).

Today: the user arranges the panels by hand. The application has no command to save an arrangement or to load one.

Open points for the worker (record each choice in `docs/decisions/`):

- one saved setup, or several named setups;
- where the setup is stored (the application settings, not the project file, is the recommended default);
- whether the last arrangement loads automatically at the next start;
- a "reset to default" command.

Rules that apply: a change from the UI is a command (AGENTS.md "Everything Is a Command"); a panel arrangement is UI state, thus decide and record whether it is undoable. A corrupt or old saved setup must load the default arrangement with a diagnostic. It must not crash.

Done means: the user saves a panel setup, changes the arrangement, loads the saved setup, and gets the saved arrangement again, also after a restart. A test in the structural suite pins the round trip (open panels, attachment, size).
